            "text": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef main():\n    # Load vectors\n    vectors = np.load(\"vectors.npy\")\n\n    # Cast to float64 for numerical precision and prevent overflow\n    vectors_64 = vectors.astype(np.float64)\n\n    # Compute squared L2 norms of each vector\n    sq_norms = np.sum(vectors_64**2, axis=1)\n\n    # Compute Gram matrix G = X @ X.T using BLAS\n    # Distances squared: ||x_i - x_j||^2 = ||x_i||^2 + ||x_j||^2 - 2 <x_i, x_j>\n    dists_sq = vectors_64 @ vectors_64.T\n    dists_sq *= -2.0\n    dists_sq += sq_norms[:, None]\n    dists_sq += sq_norms[None, :]\n\n    # Numerical stability: clamp small negative values to 0.0 and zero out diagonal\n    np.maximum(dists_sq, 0.0, out=dists_sq)\n    np.fill_diagonal(dists_sq, 0.0)\n\n    # Compute Euclidean distances and their sum\n    np.sqrt(dists_sq, out=dists_sq)\n    total_dist = float(dists_sq.sum())\n\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total_dist}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
